<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's ministry opposes BOK's supervisory power.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's ministry opposes BOK's supervisory power.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's finance ministry said on Friday it opposed allowing the central Bank of Korea (BOK) to retain the authority to supervise banks.</p>
<p>&quot;Reforms that Britain, Japan and other advanced nations are promoting in their financial supervisory systems can be good references to us,&quot; said finance minister Kang Kyong-shik in a statement.</p>
<p>Ministry officials said Kang's remarks should be interpreted as strong opposition to the central bank's supervisory right because those industrial nations favoured separation of the power from the bank.</p>
</text>
